[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

1. d4 { Perform the same movements as in the previous chapter :) } 1... d5 2. c4 { WAITING! Don't play 2.c6 here, instead, you should play 2.e6 } { [%cal Ge7e6] } 2... e6 { This is a classic way to play against the Queen's Gambit. } 3. Nc3 { [%cal Gg8f6] } 3... Nf6 4. Nf3 { Now, play 4.c6 } { [%cal Gc7c6] } 4... c6 { What characterizes the Semi-Slav defense 4 .... c6 is the move c6. If done on move 2 the variant is called Slav Defense, and if done later it is called Semi-Slav.
The Semi-Slav defense is more solid than the Slav Defense and because of the formation that your pawns adopt, it means that White has no attack options, but the downside is that your bishop on c8 is locked in. } *

